      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a7ac88bf5a5c52c08064fb9|full_name}: https://vrchat.com/home/launch?worldId=wrld_de3400c4-491f-4506-b8e8-71f06b4660bb\nHere's an example world.\nWhen you first load in it's fine, but the more people that join the worse it gets, no matter how long you've been in the world. And only to who ever is holding the \"Host\" for the room. If you leave and come back, it passes to someone else, much like the Voice Studder that happened before they fixed that. It's very noticeable on both Vr and Desktop. For that game world, we have to have someone afk in the lobby before joining to pass off this weird lag issue. I've seen it a few other times in other worlds, but I don't recall which ones.",
      "viewerReactions": null
